---
import ResponsiveImage from "../media/ResponsiveImage.astro";
import ArrowIcon from "../media/ArrowIcon.astro";
import { homeMedia } from "../../content/media";
import { liveSitePath } from "../../lib/urls";
---

<section class="power section section--navy" id="power">
  <div class="page-shell power__grid">
    <article class="power__overview" data-reveal>
      <ResponsiveImage
        image={homeMedia.electricalCapacity}
        alt="Engineers testing commercial electrical distribution equipment"
        class="power__image"
        sizes="(max-width: 61rem) calc(100vw - 2rem), 45vw"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <div class="power__shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="power__content">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Power before hardware</p>
        <h2>Can your site support commercial EV charging?</h2>
        <p>
          Existing demand, available capacity, charging windows and future expansion all affect the right solution. GreenDawn assesses those constraints before treating a network upgrade as the default answer.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Existing supply and site demand</li>
          <li>Dynamic load management</li>
          <li>DNO and IDNO coordination</li>
          <li>Future phases and expansion</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="power__decisions" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Make the power decision deliberately</p>
      <h2>Use what you have. Understand what you need.</h2>
      <p>
        The objective is a charging system that meets the operational requirement without creating unnecessary infrastructure work or restricting the next phase of the estate.
      </p>
      <div><span>01</span><strong>Assess capacity</strong><small>Understand the existing electrical position</small></div>
      <div><span>02</span><strong>Manage demand</strong><small>Use load management where it fits the operation</small></div>
      <div><span>03</span><strong>Plan the connection route</strong><small>Coordinate network work where additional power is genuinely needed</small></div>
      <a class="button button--navy" href={liveSitePath("/guides/can-my-building-handle-ev-charging/")}>Explore site power planning <ArrowIcon direction="up-right" /></a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
